    "A right triangle has a hypotenuse of 20 and one leg of 12. What is the length of the other leg?": "Use the Pythagorean theorem, leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. The known leg squared is 144, and the hypotenuse squared is 400. Subtract to isolate the missing leg: 400 minus 144 is 256. The square root of 256 is 16, so that's the other leg.",
    "Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. If one angle measures 105°, what does its alternate interior angle measure?": "Alternate interior angles formed when a transversal crosses parallel lines are always congruent — equal — to each other, so this angle also measures 105 degrees.",
    "In an isosceles triangle, the two base angles are each 48°. What does the vertex angle measure?": "All three angles of a triangle add up to 180, and here the two base angles are equal. Subtract both base angles from 180: 180 minus 48 minus 48 is 84 degrees.",
    "Angle A and Angle B are supplementary. If Angle A is 5 times Angle B, what is Angle B?": "Supplementary angles add up to 180 degrees. Since A is 5 times B, replace A with 5B: 5B plus B is 6B, and that has to equal 180. Divide 180 by 6, and B is 30 degrees.",
