    "A right triangle has a hypotenuse of 29 and one leg of 20. What is the length of the other leg?": "Use the Pythagorean theorem, leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. The known leg squared is 400, and the hypotenuse squared is 841. Subtract to isolate the missing leg: 841 minus 400 is 441. The square root of 441 is 21, so that's the other leg.",
