    "A ladder leans against a wall, forming a right triangle with the ground. The ladder (hypotenuse) is 25 ft, and the base is 7 ft from the wall. How high up the wall does the ladder reach?": "Use the Pythagorean theorem with the height as the missing leg: leg squared plus height squared equals hypotenuse squared. 49 plus height squared equals 625, so height squared is 625 minus 49, which is 576. The square root of 576 is 24, so the height is 24 feet.",
