    "A sector of a circle has a central angle of 90° and the circle has radius 8. What is the area of the sector? (Use π)": "A sector's area is just a fraction of the whole circle's area — the fraction being the sector's angle out of the full 360 degrees. A 90-degree sector is one-fourth of the circle. The full circle's area is pi times 8 squared, which is 64 pi. Take one-fourth of that, and the sector's area is 16 pi.",
