    "A square has an area of 225 square units. What is the length of one side?": "A square's area is its side length squared, so work backward: what number squared gives 225? That's 15, so each side measures 15.",
    "A square has an area of 256 square units. What is the length of one side?": "A square's area is its side length squared, so work backward: what number squared gives 256? That's 16, so each side measures 16.",
    "A square has an area of 289 square units. What is the length of one side?": "A square's area is its side length squared, so work backward: what number squared gives 289? That's 17, so each side measures 17.",
    "A square has an area of 324 square units. What is the length of one side?": "A square's area is its side length squared, so work backward: what number squared gives 324? That's 18, so each side measures 18.",
    "What is the area of a triangle with base 18 and height 5?": "A triangle's area is one-half times base times height. One-half times 18 times 5 is 45.",
    "What is the area of a triangle with base 22 and height 7?": "A triangle's area is one-half times base times height. One-half times 22 times 7 is 77.",
